    {
      "id": "n29rjb2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important District Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Original 7 districts formed in 1966 can be remembered using the mnemonic 'GHAR JK MEIN' (Gurugram, Hisar, Ambala, Rohtak, Jind, Karnal, Mahendragarh).",
        "Charkhi Dadri was carved out of Bhiwani district to become the 22nd district in 2016.",
        "Faridabad has the highest population density and maximum population among all districts."
      ],
      "id": "76vz8qe"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Haryana was carved out of Punjab on 1 November 1966 as the 17th state of India with 7 initial districts.",
        "At present, Haryana comprises 22 districts, with Charkhi Dadri being created in 2016 as the 22nd district.",
        "Sirsa is the largest district of Haryana by geographical area, while Faridabad is the smallest.",
        "Faridabad is the most populous district, whereas Panchkula has the lowest population count.",
        "Jind district is known as the 'Heart of Haryana' and shares its borders with the maximum number of other districts."
      ],
      "id": "aq31i47"
    },
